# Student Privacy

- Never publicly expose student emails, profiles, attendance, private rosters,
  private club media, precise home addresses, or other student/private-club data.
- Collect only necessary data. Use `under_13`, `age_13_17`, and `adult` governance
  bands instead of birth dates unless legally required.
- Keep under-13 self-registration disabled; require school-managed or
  guardian-authorized onboarding.
- Record and enforce relevant consent, including media consent.
- Do not add open direct messaging between minors or arbitrary PII exports.
- Private media is private by default and requires authorized signed access.
- Do not claim automatic COPPA or FERPA compliance; state that institutional and
  legal review remains required.
